# Public-Access Computer Systems: The Next Generation of Library Automation Systems.

**Authors:** Bailey, Charles W., Jr.

## Abstract
Describes nine categories of library automation systems intended for direct use by library patrons: catalog information systems; electronic information systems; information presentation systems; instructional systems; consultation systems; information services and delivery systems; conferencing systems; integrative systems; and user computing facilities. The need to integrate these systems with traditional collections and services is discussed. (32 references) (CLB)

